    "debrief": {
      "scope": "Every host in VLAN 10: no address at all, other VLANs fine",
      "methods": [
        "follow_the_path",
        "compare_known_good"
      ],
      "reasoning": "Only one VLAN is affected and its hosts get no address at all, so DHCP never completes. The server sits on another subnet, so each DISCOVER depends on the VLAN's gateways relaying it. Both relays point at 10.1.10.10, an address inside the VLAN that no device owns, so the requests go nowhere. Compare with a VLAN that works: its helper is the server's address.\n",
